This guide covers core DevOps principles, essential tooling, containerization, and a complete step-by-step walkthrough to build, test, and containerize a microservice using GitHub Actions.

### 1. Core DevOps & CI/CD Concepts
What is DevOps?
DevOps is a set of cultural philosophies, practices, and tools that combines software development (Dev) and IT operations (Ops) to deliver applications at high velocity with automated reliability.

What is CI/CD?
Continuous Integration (CI): Developers commit and merge code frequently to a shared repository. Every push triggers automated builds and automated test suites. Bugs are caught immediately before code is merged.

Continuous Delivery (CD): Once CI tests pass, the application is packaged (e.g., into an immutable Docker image) and automatically deployed to staging or prepared for production release with minimal manual overhead.

Continuous Deployment (Advanced CD): Every validated change that passes all testing stages automatically releases straight to production without manual approvals.

