### 3. Deployment Strategies Overview
Recreate (Downtime): Shuts down old containers completely before launching new ones. Causes brief downtime.

Rolling Update (Zero Downtime): Progressively spins up new containers while terminating old containers one by one behind a load balancer.

Blue-Green Deployment: Maintains two identical production environments (Blue = live, Green = new build). Traffic is switched instantaneously via the router once the Green environment passes validation. Allows instant rollback if bugs emerge.

Canary Deployment: Routes a tiny percentage of live user traffic (e.g., 5%) to the new version to monitor errors and performance before rolling it out to 100% of users.

