### 6. Common Pitfalls & Solutions
GitHub Authentication & Token Scopes (Error 403 / remote rejected):

When using a Personal Access Token (PAT), ensure you check both the repo and workflow scopes. GitHub blocks pushes containing .github/workflows/ files if the token lacks explicit workflow authorization.

Pytest Module Pathing (ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'app'):

Use python -m pytest instead of plain pytest in your CI scripts. This ensures Python automatically appends the current working directory to sys.path.

Docker Layer Caching Optimization:

Always copy requirements.txt and run pip install before copying your application files (COPY app/ ./app). If only source code changes, Docker skips dependency installation and reuses the cached layer.